[265.585526, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY — Wordpress Defacement campaign\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER   Analyst handoff   Confidence: HIGH   (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: wordpress-prod-01   Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.40\r\n\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered only part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\n   T1190      Exploit Public-Facing Application          [initial-access]  step 1: WordPress plugin RCE (CVE-2022-1609)\r\n   T1505.003  Web Shell                                  [persistence]  step 2: PHP webshell planted\r\n   T1491.001  Internal Defacement                        [impact]  step 3: site defacement\r\n   T1053.003  Cron                                       [execution]  step 4: cron persistence\r\n   T1505.003  Web Shell                                  [persistence]  step 5: .htaccess redirect\r\n\r\n3. RELEVANT VULNERABILITIES (source: NVD, US-Gov public domain)\r\n   CVE-2022-1609  CVSS 9.8 (CRITICAL) v3.1  CWE=CWE-94\r\n      The School Management WordPress plugin before 9.9.7 contains an obfuscated backdoor injected in it's license checking code that registers a REST API handler, allowing an unauthenticated attacker to execute arbitrary PHP code on the site.\r\n      ref: https://wpscan.com/vulnerability/e2d546c9-85b6-47a4-b951-781b9ae5d0f2/\r\n\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\n   ip     198.51.100.40\r\n   c2     update-wordpress[.]example[.]cn\r\n   pool   stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]wordpress[.]evil[:]3333\r\n   wallet 4A0000000000000000001b88b8daaa21\r\n\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S. National Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n"]
[265.585925, "o", "==="]
[265.586008, "o", "\r\n"]
[265.586522, "o", "# CHANGE TICKET  CHG-1481  (DRAFT — reconcile against your findings)\r\n\r\n> A previous shift pre-filled this remediation ticket from the SAS alerts ALONE. It is known\r\n> to be incomplete and contains stale/incorrect lines. Correct it IN PLACE against your own\r\n> investigation of /disk; cite evidence for every change. Do not author from scratch.\r\n\r\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note |\r\n|---|--------|--------|--------|------|\r\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | 203.0.113.9 | proposed | STALE: prior shift used the wrong IP; confirm the real origin from /disk |\r\n| 2 | Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) | RDP | proposed | WRONG: not the entry vector for this host — verify against /sas/cti |\r\n| 3 | Remove cron miner | /var/spool/cron/root | DONE | UNVERIFIED: marked done with no evidence — re-check |\r\n| 4 | (add) silent persistence you discover | /var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data | TODO | ticket omits everything not alerted — add the rest |\r\n\r\n## Reviewer checklist\r\n- [ ] Every action maps to a cited artifact under /disk or /sas\r\n- [ ] Fix the wrong IP (row 1) and wrong CVE (row 2)\r\n- [ ] Downgrade row 3 from DONE to VERIFIED-or-OPEN with evidence\r\n- [ ] Add the silent (non-alerted) artifacts the prior shift missed\r\n"]
[265.586913, "o", "==="]
[265.586932, "o", "\r\n"]
