[606.319593, "o", "On August 16, 2024, endpoint security feeds surfaced initial alerts for host `wordpress-prod-01` (`/sas/alerts.json:1-25`). Specifically, alerts covered PHP webshell execution at `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` (`/sas/alerts.json:4`), site defacement at `/var/www/html/index.html` (`/sas/alerts.json:11`), and baseline weaknesses in `wp-config.php` (`/sas/alerts.json:18`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[606.319624, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[606.320186, "o", "However, forensic investigation of the disk image (`/disk`) revealed several **silent (unalerted)** post-exploitation actions and persistence mechanisms that were missed by security alerting:  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[606.320245, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[606.320348, "o", "> "]
[606.320508, "o", "1. Scheduled crontab persistence for user `www-data` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:2`).  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[606.320521, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[606.321984, "o", "2. Scheduled crontab persistence for user `root` (`/disk/etc/crontab:5`).  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 3. Malicious `.htaccess` traffic redirection to `198.51.100.40` (`/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## 2. Chronological Incident Timeline\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | Timestamp (UTC) | Category | Description | Alerted vs Silent | Citation |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 2026-08-09 03:11:17 | Exploitation | Webshell upload POST request to `/uploads/shell.php` | Alerted (ALERT-01) | `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:297`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/error.log:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:4` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 2026-08-09 03:12:49 | Reconnaissance | Attacker JNDI Log4Shell probe | **Silent (Unalerted)** | `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:298` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 2026-08-09 03:13:22 | Reconnaissance | Attacker Struts2 OGNL probe | **Silent (Unalerted)** | `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:299` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 2026-08-09 03:15:00 | Persistence | Attacker established crontab persistence | **Silent (Unalerted)** | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:2`, `/disk/etc/crontab:5` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## 3. Working Checklist & Investigation Status\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - [x] Review SAS Alert Feed & Catalog Unalerted Artifacts (`/sas/alerts.json:1`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - [x] Analyze Vendor Threat Advisory (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:1`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - [x] Web Server Log Forensic Analysis (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:297`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/error.log:1`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
